  "scope_statement": "This is a manifest-level scenario card. If the scenario file contains a Country value, that value is the scenario authoring default; the run certificate records the countries actually materialised and executed.",
  "summary": "Comprehensive blood pressure control intervention for people with diabetes to prevent cardiovascular and microvascular complications.\nThis scenario exposes the parameters for nephropathy screening and blood pressure management programs that work by early detection of kidney disease and systematic hypertension control.\nThe intervention reduces progression from diabetes to diabetic nephropathy and other cardiovascular complications by providing regular blood pressure monitoring, antihypertensive medications, and nephropathy screening.\nNephropathy screening identifies diabetic patients with early kidney damage who require enhanced blood pressure control, with a target population in need of 33% of diabetic patients.\nThe intervention includes regular blood pressure measurement, medication management with ACE inhibitors or ARBs, urine protein testing, and coordinated care to prevent kidney disease progression.\nThis intervention is critical for preventing both cardiovascular events and kidney failure in people with diabetes, addressing two major causes of morbidity and mortality.\nNote: This intervention should be implemented alongside other diabetes care interventions for comprehensive management of diabetes complications.\n",
  "title": "Appendix 3 - D5 Scenario"
}
